</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Pain Assessment Model Architecture</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Building upon our synthetic dataset, we develop a dual-branch Vision Transformer architecture that simultaneously performs PSPI classification and Action Unit regression. Our approach incorporates cross-modal knowledge distillation to leverage both synthetic facial images and heatmap representations, enabling robust pain assessment across diverse populations and imaging conditions.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Architecture</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our architecture employs a pretrained Vision Transformer (ViT-Large) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite> as the feature extraction backbone for its superior representational capacity. The model processes input images of size <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="224\times 224" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>224</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>224</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">224\times 224</annotation></semantics></math> through patch embedding, resulting in a sequence of patch tokens <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{P}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{P}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of patches and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is the hidden dimension. A learnable classification token <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{CLS}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐂𝐋𝐒</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{CLS}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is prepended to capture global facial representations.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">A dual-branch design separates PSPI classification from AU regression to accommodate their fundamentally different prediction tasks. The PSPI branch performs 17-class classification (scores 0-16), while the AU branch regresses continuous intensity values for six pain-relevant Action Units (AU4, AU6, AU7, AU9, AU10, AU43) identified in the PSPI formula <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>. Our model thus receives supervision signals from both prediction heads, enabling the shared feature representations to capture both holistic pain expressions and fine-grained facial muscle activations simultaneously (see <a href="#S2.F3" title="In 2 Related Works ‣ Pain in 3D: Generating Controllable Synthetic Faces for Automated Pain Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Query-Based AU Cross-Attention Mechanism.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Traditional approaches rely on global CLS token features for all predictions, which may dilute spatially-specific information crucial for AU detection. Inspired by recent advances in human mesh recovery <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, we introduce learnable AU-specific query tokens <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}_{AU}\in\mathbb{R}^{6\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}_{AU}\in\mathbb{R}^{6\times D}</annotation></semantics></math>, that cross-attend to patch features to extract localized facial action information (see <a href="#S4.T2" title="In Feature-Level Distillation: ‣ 4.2 Cross-Modal Knowledge Distillation ‣ 4 Pain Assessment Model Architecture ‣ Pain in 3D: Generating Controllable Synthetic Faces for Automated Pain Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>):</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{A}_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{A}_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbf{Q}_{AU_{i}}\mathbf{P}_{j}^{T}}{\sqrt{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbf{Q}_{AU_{i}}\mathbf{P}_{j}^{T}}{\sqrt{D}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\exp(\mathbf{A}_{i,j})}{\sum_{k=1}^{N}\exp(\mathbf{A}_{i,k})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\exp(\mathbf{A}_{i,j})}{\sum_{k=1}^{N}\exp(\mathbf{A}_{i,k})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{F}_{AU_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{F}_{AU_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{N}\alpha_{i,j}\mathbf{P}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{j=1}^{N}\alpha_{i,j}\mathbf{P}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{F}_{AU_{i}}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{F}_{AU_{i}}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the attended feature for AU <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. This cross-attention mechanism allows each AU query to focus on relevant facial regions specific to the action units query <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}_{AU_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}_{AU_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The AU predictions are computed as:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{H}_{AU}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{H}_{AU}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{ReLU}(\text{Linear}(\mathbf{F}_{AU}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>ReLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Linear</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{ReLU}(\text{Linear}(\mathbf{F}_{AU}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{AU}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{AU}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{ReLU}(\text{Linear}(\mathbf{H}_{AU}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>ReLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Linear</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{ReLU}(\text{Linear}(\mathbf{H}_{AU}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">where ReLU ensures non-negative AU intensities consistent with clinical interpretation, and <math id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{AU}\in\mathbb{R}^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{AU}\in\mathbb{R}^{6}</annotation></semantics></math> contains the predicted AU values.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PSPI Classification Branch.</span>
The PSPI classification branch utilizes the global CLS token for pain intensity prediction:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{H}_{PSPI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{H}_{PSPI}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{LayerNorm}(\mathbf{CLS})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>LayerNorm</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐂𝐋𝐒</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{LayerNorm}(\mathbf{CLS})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{H}_{PSPI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{H}_{PSPI}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Dropout}(\text{GELU}(\text{Linear}(\mathbf{H}_{PSPI})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Dropout</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>GELU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Linear</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Dropout}(\text{GELU}(\text{Linear}(\mathbf{H}_{PSPI})))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbf{H}_{PSPI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbf{H}_{PSPI}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Dropout}(\text{GELU}(\text{Linear}(\mathbf{H}_{PSPI})))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Dropout</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>GELU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>Linear</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Dropout}(\text{GELU}(\text{Linear}(\mathbf{H}_{PSPI})))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{PSPI}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{PSPI}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Linear}(\mathbf{H}_{PSPI})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>Linear</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐇</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Linear}(\mathbf{H}_{PSPI})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The architecture includes progressive dimensionality reduction with dropout regularization to prevent overfitting while maintaining sufficient capacity for the 17-class classification task.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Cross-Modal Knowledge Distillation</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To leverage complementary information from different modalities, we implement a three-level distillation framework that transfers knowledge from a teacher model trained on heatmap representations to our student model operating on synthetic facial images (see <a href="#S2.F3" title="In 2 Related Works ‣ Pain in 3D: Generating Controllable Synthetic Faces for Automated Pain Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Output-Level Distillation:</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We employ KL divergence for PSPI classification knowledge transfer:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{PSPI}}^{\text{distill}}=T^{2}\,\mathrm{KL}\left(\text{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathbf{z}_{t}}{T}\right)\,\left\|\,\text{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathbf{z}_{s}}{T}\right)\right.\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>PSPI</mtext><mtext>distill</mtext></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtext>softmax</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">‖</mo><mtext>softmax</mtext><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{PSPI}}^{\text{distill}}=T^{2}\,\mathrm{KL}\left(\text{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathbf{z}_{t}}{T}\right)\,\left\|\,\text{softmax}\left(\frac{\mathbf{z}_{s}}{T}\right)\right.\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{z}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{z}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are the softmaxed outputs of the student and teacher, and <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> is the temperature. As for AU regression, we distill heatmap knowledge with Mean Squared Error:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{AU}^{distill}=\text{MSE}(\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{AU}^{student},\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{AU}^{teacher})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>MSE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{AU}^{distill}=\text{MSE}(\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{AU}^{student},\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{AU}^{teacher})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Feature-Level Distillation:</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We align the CLS token representations between student and teacher models:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{feature}^{distill}=\text{MSE}(\mathbf{CLS}^{student},\mathbf{CLS}^{teacher})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>MSE</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝐂𝐋𝐒</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐂𝐋𝐒</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{feature}^{distill}=\text{MSE}(\mathbf{CLS}^{student},\mathbf{CLS}^{teacher})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This guides the student to learn task-relevant representations similar to the teacher, despite differing input modalities (e.g., images vs. heatmaps). By mimicking the teacher’s CLS token, the student inherits a global understanding of facial pain and expression patterns, capturing correlations across action units and overall pain intensity (see <a href="#S4.T2" title="In Feature-Level Distillation: ‣ 4.2 Cross-Modal Knowledge Distillation ‣ 4 Pain Assessment Model Architecture ‣ Pain in 3D: Generating Controllable Synthetic Faces for Automated Pain Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Loss Formulation.</span> The total training loss combines supervised learning objectives with distillation terms:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{total}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{total}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\lambda_{PSPI}\,\mathcal{L}_{CE}(\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{PSPI},\mathbf{y}_{PSPI})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\lambda_{PSPI}\,\mathcal{L}_{CE}(\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{PSPI},\mathbf{y}_{PSPI})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\lambda_{AU}\,\mathcal{L}_{MSE}(\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{AU},\mathbf{y}_{AU})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐲</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐲</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\lambda_{AU}\,\mathcal{L}_{MSE}(\hat{\mathbf{y}}_{AU},\mathbf{y}_{AU})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\lambda_{PSPI}^{distill}\,\mathcal{L}_{PSPI}^{distill}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\lambda_{PSPI}^{distill}\,\mathcal{L}_{PSPI}^{distill}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\lambda_{AU}^{distill}\,\mathcal{L}_{AU}^{distill}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\lambda_{AU}^{distill}\,\mathcal{L}_{AU}^{distill}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\lambda_{feature}^{distill}\,\mathcal{L}_{feature}^{distill}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\lambda_{feature}^{distill}\,\mathcal{L}_{feature}^{distill}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{CE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{CE}</annotation></semantics></math> is the cross-entropy loss for PSPI classification, and <math id="S4.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> terms are hyperparameters controlling the relative importance of each loss component.</p>
</div>
